@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+# Summary: `--format markdown`
+
+## What changed
+- `stockreport/report.py`: `render()` accepts `fmt="markdown"`. It renders the same rows and columns as the text report using the vendored tabulate's `style="pipe"` (GitHub-flavoured markdown), with `number_format=".2f"`, then appends a blank line and `**Total stock value:** <value>`.
+- `stockreport/__main__.py`: `--format` now accepts `markdown` as well as `text`.
+- `README.md`: documents the new option.
+
+No tests were edited or added; the existing `test_markdown_output` and `test_cli_markdown` in `tests/test_report.py` cover the change. `vendor/` and dependencies are untouched.
+
+## Verification
+- `python -m unittest -v` before the change: 1 failure, 1 error (the two markdown tests). After the change: `Ran 3 tests ... OK`, all three passing.
+- `python -m stockreport inventory.csv --format markdown` prints the table and total as expected.
+- Checked the vendored tabulate's `pipe` output directly; it matches the expected test output byte-for-byte.
+
+## Not verified / caveats
+- Only the sample `inventory.csv` was exercised. Item names containing `|` would break the markdown table, since no escaping is done. The vendored tabulate has no escape option, so I did not handle this.
+- Right-alignment of the Qty and Unit price columns comes from tabulate's default numeric alignment; it matches the test, but I did not check other data shapes.
+- Not checked on the locked-down warehouse machines (only this environment).
